Input: {"question": "Who was Chilperic's father?", "original_source_segments": {"D1S1": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0393-b57e59f62da2:d00", "start": 0, "end": 27, "text": "Chilperic I Chilperic I (c."}, "D1S2": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0393-b57e59f62da2:d00", "start": 28, "end": 110, "text": "539 – September 584) was the king of Neustria (or Soissons) from 561 to his death."}, "D1S3": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0393-b57e59f62da2:d00", "start": 111, "end": 184, "text": "He was one of the sons of the Frankish king Clotaire I and Queen Aregund."}, "D1S4": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0393-b57e59f62da2:d00", "start": 185, "end": 364, "text": "Immediately after the death of his father in 561, he endeavoured to take possession of the whole kingdom, seized the treasure amassed in the royal town of Berny and entered Paris."}, "D1S5": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0393-b57e59f62da2:d00", "start": 365, "end": 547, "text": "His brothers, however, compelled him to divide the kingdom with them, and Soissons, together with Amiens, Arras, Cambrai, Thérouanne, Tournai, and Boulogne fell to Chilperic's share."}, "D1S6": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0393-b57e59f62da2:d00", "start": 548, "end": 596, "text": "His eldest brother Charibert received Paris, the"}, "D2S1": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0393-b57e59f62da2:d01", "start": 0, "end": 172, "text": "instigation of Chilperic ’ s concubine Fredegund , our ancestor , who then became Chilperic ’ s third wife , at the beginning of 40 years of brutal warfare with Brunhilde ."}, "D2S2": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0393-b57e59f62da2:d01", "start": 173, "end": 247, "text": "See http : //en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chilperic_I for lots more information ."}, "D2S3": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0393-b57e59f62da2:d01", "start": 248, "end": 366, "text": "-- -- -- -- -- -- -- -- -- -- http : //en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chilperic_II_of_Burgundy -- -- -- -- -- -- -- -- -- -- d."}, "D2S4": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0393-b57e59f62da2:d01", "start": 367, "end": 431, "text": "584 , Frankish king of Neustria ( 561–84 ) , son of Clotaire I ."}, "D2S5": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0393-b57e59f62da2:d01", "start": 432, "end": 537, "text": "He feuded bitterly with his brother Sigebert I , who had inherited the E Frankish kingdom that came to be"}, "D3S1": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0393-b57e59f62da2:d02", "start": 0, "end": 19, "text": "Known as Austrasia."}, "D3S2": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0393-b57e59f62da2:d02", "start": 20, "end": 212, "text": "Their struggle became savage after Chilperic and his mistress and future wife, Fredegunde, murdered (567) Chilperic’s second wife, Galswintha; she was the sister of Sigebert’s wife, Brunhilda."}, "D3S3": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0393-b57e59f62da2:d02", "start": 213, "end": 300, "text": "In the wars between the two brothers, Sigebert overran Neustria before his death (575)."}, "D3S4": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0393-b57e59f62da2:d02", "start": 301, "end": 373, "text": "Later, Chilperic was murdered, probably at the instigation of Brunhilda."}, "D3S5": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0393-b57e59f62da2:d02", "start": 374, "end": 443, "text": "The feud was inherited by Chilperic’s son and successor, Clotaire II."}, "D3S6": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0393-b57e59f62da2:d02", "start": 444, "end": 538, "text": "Chilperic was the son of Lothair I, who had divided the kingdom among his sons upon his death."}, "D3S7": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0393-b57e59f62da2:d02", "start": 539, "end": 580, "text": "The Columbia Encyclopedia, Sixth Edition."}, "D3S8": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0393-b57e59f62da2:d02", "start": 581, "end": 586, "text": "2001."}, "D4S1": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0393-b57e59f62da2:d03", "start": 0, "end": 234, "text": "Subsequent marriage to Fredegund produced four more legitimate offspring: Samson, died young; Rigunth, betrothed to Reccared but never married; Theuderic, died young; Clotaire, his successor in Neustria, later sole king of the Franks."}, "D4S2": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0393-b57e59f62da2:d03", "start": 235, "end": 250, "text": "Chilperic I (c."}, "D4S3": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0393-b57e59f62da2:d03", "start": 251, "end": 333, "text": "539 – September 584) was the king of Neustria (or Soissons) from 561 to his death."}, "D4S4": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0393-b57e59f62da2:d03", "start": 334, "end": 381, "text": "He was one of the sons of Guntram, and Aregund."}, "D4S5": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0393-b57e59f62da2:d03", "start": 382, "end": 427, "text": "Chilperic I's first marriage was to Audovera."}, "D4S6": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0393-b57e59f62da2:d03", "start": 428, "end": 463, "text": "They had four children: Theudebert."}, "D5S1": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0393-b57e59f62da2:d04", "start": 0, "end": 103, "text": "Chilperic II of Burgundy Chilperic II (; 450–493 AD) was the King of Burgundy from 473 until his death."}, "D5S2": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0393-b57e59f62da2:d04", "start": 104, "end": 169, "text": "Before that he co-ruled with his father Gondioc beginning in 463."}, "D5S3": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0393-b57e59f62da2:d04", "start": 170, "end": 395, "text": "He began his reign in 473 after the partition of Burgundy with his younger brothers Godegisel, Gundobad, and Godomar; he ruled from \"Valentia Julia\" (Valence) and his brothers ruled respectively from Geneva, Vienne, and Lyon."}, "D5S4": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0393-b57e59f62da2:d04", "start": 396, "end": 533, "text": "Sometime in the early 470s Chilperic was forced to submit to the authority of the Roman Empire by the \"magister militum\" Ecdicius Avitus."}, "D5S5": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0393-b57e59f62da2:d04", "start": 534, "end": 605, "text": "In 475 he probably sheltered an exiled Ecdicius after the Visigoths had"}, "D6S1": {"document_number": 6, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0393-b57e59f62da2:d05", "start": 0, "end": 29, "text": "Chilperic II Chilperic II (c."}, "D6S2": {"document_number": 6, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0393-b57e59f62da2:d05", "start": 30, "end": 232, "text": "672 – 13 February 721), known as Daniel prior to his coronation, was the youngest son of Childeric II and his half-cousin, king of Neustria from 715 and sole king of the Franks from 718 until his death."}, "D6S3": {"document_number": 6, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0393-b57e59f62da2:d05", "start": 233, "end": 341, "text": "As an infant, he was spirited to a monastery to protect his life from the internecine feuding of his family."}, "D6S4": {"document_number": 6, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0393-b57e59f62da2:d05", "start": 342, "end": 530, "text": "There, he was raised as Daniel until the death of Dagobert III in 715, when he was taken from the monastery — at the age of forty-three — and raised on the shield of the Neustrian warriors"}, "D7S1": {"document_number": 7, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0393-b57e59f62da2:d06", "start": 0, "end": 517, "text": "II ( 629–632 ) Chilperic ( 632 ) Sigebert III ( 634–656 ) Childebert the Adopted ( 656–661 ) Clovis II ( 639–657 ) Chlothar III ( 657–673 ) Childeric II ( 662–675 ) Theuderic III ( 675–691 ) Dagobert II ( 675–679 ) Clovis IV ( 691–695 ) Childebert III ( 695–711 ) Dagobert III ( 711–715 ) Chilperic II ( 715–721 ) Chlothar IV ( 717–720 ) Theuderic IV ( 721–737 ) Childeric III ( 743–751 ) v t e Monarchs of France Detailed family tree Simplified family tree List of Frankish kings List of French monarchs Merovingians"}, "D8S1": {"document_number": 8, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0393-b57e59f62da2:d07", "start": 0, "end": 94, "text": "article incorporates text from a publication now in the public domain : Chisholm , Hugh , ed ."}, "D8S2": {"document_number": 8, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0393-b57e59f62da2:d07", "start": 95, "end": 105, "text": "( 1911 ) ."}, "D8S3": {"document_number": 8, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0393-b57e59f62da2:d07", "start": 106, "end": 123, "text": "`` Childeric `` ."}, "D8S4": {"document_number": 8, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0393-b57e59f62da2:d07", "start": 124, "end": 158, "text": "Encyclopædia Britannica ( 11th ed."}, "D8S5": {"document_number": 8, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0393-b57e59f62da2:d07", "start": 159, "end": 162, "text": ") ."}, "D8S6": {"document_number": 8, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0393-b57e59f62da2:d07", "start": 163, "end": 191, "text": "Cambridge University Press ."}, "D8S7": {"document_number": 8, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0393-b57e59f62da2:d07", "start": 192, "end": 226, "text": "Sources edit Bachrach , Bernard S."}, "D8S8": {"document_number": 8, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0393-b57e59f62da2:d07", "start": 227, "end": 248, "text": "; Bachrach , David S."}, "D8S9": {"document_number": 8, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0393-b57e59f62da2:d07", "start": 249, "end": 277, "text": "; Leese , Michael ( 2018 ) ."}, "D8S10": {"document_number": 8, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0393-b57e59f62da2:d07", "start": 278, "end": 340, "text": "Deeds of the Bishops of Cambrai , Translation and Commentary ."}, "D8S11": {"document_number": 8, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0393-b57e59f62da2:d07", "start": 341, "end": 352, "text": "Routledge ."}, "D8S12": {"document_number": 8, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0393-b57e59f62da2:d07", "start": 353, "end": 373, "text": "ISBN 9781317036210 ."}, "D8S13": {"document_number": 8, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0393-b57e59f62da2:d07", "start": 374, "end": 536, "text": "External links edit Media related to Childeric II at Wikimedia Commons Childeric II Merovingian dynasty Born : 653 Died : 675 Preceded by Chlothar III King of the"}, "D9S1": {"document_number": 9, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0393-b57e59f62da2:d08", "start": 0, "end": 111, "text": "zijn eerste vrouw Audovera kreeg hij vijf kinderen : Theodebert , Merovech , Clovis , Basina en Childeswindis ."}, "D9S2": {"document_number": 9, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0393-b57e59f62da2:d08", "start": 112, "end": 287, "text": "Hoewel hij ook met zijn bijzit Fredegonde leefde - zij was van lagere afkomst en tevens zijn boze geest - wou hij , zoals zijn broer Sigebert I , ook met een prinses trouwen ."}, "D9S3": {"document_number": 9, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0393-b57e59f62da2:d08", "start": 288, "end": 357, "text": "Het werd Galswintha , de oudere halfzus van Brunhilde van Austrasië ."}, "D9S4": {"document_number": 9, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0393-b57e59f62da2:d08", "start": 358, "end": 484, "text": "Toen deze zag dat haar man Fredegonde niet kon loslaten , wou zij haar man verlaten en naar haar vaderland Spanje terugkeren ."}, "D9S5": {"document_number": 9, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0393-b57e59f62da2:d08", "start": 485, "end": 520, "text": "De bruidsschat mocht hij behouden ."}, "D9S6": {"document_number": 9, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0393-b57e59f62da2:d08", "start": 521, "end": 543, "text": "Op een morgen vond men"}}, "original_cards": [{"doc_id": "ramdocs-0393-b57e59f62da2:d00", "card_id": "ramdocs-0393-b57e59f62da2:d00:c0", "entity": "Chilperic I", "scope": "Parentage", "claim": "Chilperic I was one of the sons of the Frankish king Clotaire I.", "answer": "Clotaire I", "quote": "He was one of the sons of the Frankish king Clotaire I and Queen Aregund.", "original_document_number": 1}, {"doc_id": "ramdocs-0393-b57e59f62da2:d01", "card_id": "ramdocs-0393-b57e59f62da2:d01:c0", "entity": "Chilperic", "scope": "Frankish king of Neustria", "claim": "Chilperic, Frankish king of Neustria (561–84), was the son of Clotaire I.", "answer": "Clotaire I", "quote": "584 , Frankish king of Neustria ( 561–84 ) , son of Clotaire I .", "original_document_number": 2}, {"doc_id": "ramdocs-0393-b57e59f62da2:d02", "card_id": "ramdocs-0393-b57e59f62da2:d02:c0", "entity": "Chilperic", "scope": "Parentage", "claim": "Chilperic was the son of Lothair I.", "answer": "Lothair I", "quote": "Chilperic was the son of Lothair I, who had divided the kingdom among his sons upon his death.", "original_document_number": 3}, {"doc_id": "ramdocs-0393-b57e59f62da2:d03", "card_id": "ramdocs-0393-b57e59f62da2:d03:c0", "entity": "Chilperic I", "scope": "Parentage", "claim": "Chilperic I was one of the sons of Guntram and Aregund.", "answer": "Guntram and Aregund", "quote": "He was one of the sons of Guntram, and Aregund.", "original_document_number": 4}, {"doc_id": "ramdocs-0393-b57e59f62da2:d04", "card_id": "ramdocs-0393-b57e59f62da2:d04:c0", "entity": "Chilperic II", "scope": "King of Burgundy", "claim": "Chilperic II co-ruled with his father Gondioc beginning in 463.", "answer": "Gondioc", "quote": "Before that he co-ruled with his father Gondioc beginning in 463.", "original_document_number": 5}, {"doc_id": "ramdocs-0393-b57e59f62da2:d05", "card_id": "ramdocs-0393-b57e59f62da2:d05:c0", "entity": "Chilperic II", "scope": "Parentage", "claim": "Chilperic II was the youngest son of Childeric II.", "answer": "Childeric II", "quote": "672 – 13 February 721), known as Daniel prior to his coronation, was the youngest son of Childeric II and his half-cousin, king of Neustria from 715 and sole king of the Franks from 718 until his death.", "original_document_number": 6}], "current_answers": ["Clotaire I", "Lothair I", "Guntram", "Gondioc", "Childeric II"], "candidate_answers": [{"candidate_id": "R0", "answer": "Clotaire I", "origin": "initial"}, {"candidate_id": "R1", "answer": "Lothair I", "origin": "initial"}, {"candidate_id": "R2", "answer": "Guntram", "origin": "initial"}, {"candidate_id": "R3", "answer": "Gondioc", "origin": "coverage_addition"}, {"candidate_id": "R4", "answer": "Childeric II", "origin": "coverage_addition"}]}

